From skeid #29 review M5: Skeid.pm:1624 key_id_for_key derives the customer key id as a short truncated digest; it is the sole separator of customers' routing, billing and (since #29) manifests. Collision/guessing margin is thin. Options: widen the digest (e.g. full SHA-256 hex or >=128 bits), or keyed HMAC with a server secret (prevents offline mapping key->id); both change existing ids -> migration for stored usage events and config keys: sections (accept old ids for a transition, document re-issue). Needs a decision + skeid ADR.
